  "data": {
    "body": "Which of the following statements is always TRUE? (All matrices are real matrices.)\n\n\n\n(i) If $A$ is a symmetric matrix, then $A$ always has $n$ distinct eigenvalues.\n\n(ii) If $A$ is symmetric, then $A^{2}$ is orthogonally diagonalizable.\n\n(iii) If both $A$ and $B$ are orthogonally diagonalizable, then so is $A B$.\n\n(iv) If $A$ is symmetric, then any two eigenvectors from different eigenspaces are orthogonal.",
